Comment to code suggestions


slash commands:
/explain (you can select your code and type in copilot chat or inline chat)
/refactor (It will optimize your code and provide best code suggestion)
/tests (It will generate test cases with new file )
/docs or /doc - Generate or improve documentation for code
/fix - Attempt to fix errors or bugs in the selected code
/optimize - Optimize the selected code for performance or readability
/generate - Create new code based on a description or requirements
/run - Execute code or tests (if supported by the environment)
/comment - add or improve comments in the code
/summarize - provide the summary of the code or file
/help - help command in GitHub Copilot shows you the list of available Copilot chat commands,
      explains what each command does, and helps you understand how to use Copilot features inside the chat.
/setuptests is a slash command in GitHub Copilot Chat that helps you set up a test framework and basic test structure for your project.
            It is used when you don’t have tests yet or when your project’s test environment is not configured.
/clear - It will clear the chat history


Limitations of Github Copilot:
Copilot wont give 100% correctness of code or suggestions: Developer needs to verify those.
If you have more lines of code like 10000 and ask copilot to explain it truncates and explains because copilot has context limitaions and token limitations so it 
   cannot summarize huge huge lines of code
